│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ balanced_twohop                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This surrogate keeps the useful direct-demand signal, then adds a conservative reward for │
│                          │ pairs of links that form a two-hop route. The two-hop reward is scaled by the demand’s    │
│                          │ row and column traffic levels, so it does not treat every possible intermediate node as   │
│                          │ equally attractive. A smaller node-traffic term favors links incident to nodes likely to  │
│                          │ need transit capacity. Coefficients are normalized together, and the quadratic term count │
│                          │ is at most \(n(n-1)(n-2)\), within the stated limit. This is a routing-inspired           │
│                          │ approximation rather than an exact prediction of the routing LP.                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
