│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tempered_two_hop_routing                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a modest reward when two selected links form a two-hop route for a demanded           │
│                          │ origin-destination pair. This gives the QUBO a signal for useful indirect connectivity,   │
│                          │ which the direct-demand baseline misses, while tempering the naive two-hop reward known   │
│                          │ to perform poorly. Dividing the reward by the square root of the number of possible       │
│                          │ intermediates limits the aggregate incentive as the network grows. The construction uses  │
│                          │ at most n(n−1)(n−2) quadratic terms and leaves degree penalties to the evaluator.         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
