│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses only a linear reward for direct demand and has no pairwise      │
│                          │ terms. This version keeps direct demand as the main signal, but slightly tempers its      │
│                          │ largest values and adds a small normalized transit-centrality signal. It adds modest      │
│                          │ rewards for two-link routes and for pairs of useful links sharing a source or             │
│                          │ destination, plus a mild penalty for low-value reciprocal links. These terms provide      │
│                          │ routing and link-selection context without letting two-hop rewards dominate. The          │
│                          │ resulting quadratic-term count is below the \(4n^3\) limit; the degree penalty is set to  │
│                          │ 1.5.                                                                                      │
