│ patch_name               │ transit_congestion                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current two-hop terms reward every selected two-link path, which can favor topologies │
│                          │ that route traffic through the same busy intermediaries. Replace that reward with a       │
│                          │ modest positive congestion cost: selecting both links of a path incurs more cost when its │
│                          │ demand is high and the intermediate node has heavy inbound or outbound traffic. This      │
│                          │ retains the direct-demand signal while discouraging especially risky transit paths,       │
│                          │ without exceeding the existing O(n³) term count.                                          │
