│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ relay_capacity_surrogate                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This surrogate estimates whether a node is a useful relay from the balance between        │
│                          │ traffic entering and leaving it, rather than from its total load. It rewards direct links │
│                          │ for their own demand and adds sparse, demand-conditioned rewards for pairs of links that  │
│                          │ form a two-hop route. The relay factor favors nodes with capacity on both sides of a      │
│                          │ route, while the path reward is reduced when the direct demand is already well served by  │
│                          │ its direct-link term. This provides a different transit profile while keeping the         │
│                          │ interaction set to at most O(n³).                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
