│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ transit_fit                                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces the direct-demand-plus-generic-path-reward model with a demand-conditioned  │
│                          │ transit-fit model. For each origin–destination pair, it scores candidate two-hop routes   │
│                          │ according to how strongly the intermediate node is connected to that particular origin    │
│                          │ and destination, rather than using a broad node-traffic statistic. It also retains a      │
│                          │ modest direct-link preference and discounts transit choices at nodes with high aggregate  │
│                          │ traffic. The resulting interactions remain restricted to two-hop paths, keeping the term  │
│                          │ count within the limit while aiming to make useful routes more prominent in both the best │
│                          │ and typical low-energy samples.                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
