│ patch_name               │ unaveraged_twohop_reward                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the per-intermediate averaging and node-congestion discount with a modest,        │
│                          │ uniform reward for each demand-supported two-hop path. The current factors make each      │
│                          │ quadratic coefficient especially small, so these terms may have little influence relative │
│                          │ to direct-link rewards. Using `-0.08 * demand / scale` keeps the same sparse set of       │
│                          │ interactions while giving selected paths a stronger signal. The coefficient is            │
│                          │ deliberately well below the previously tried strong two-hop reward, which performed worse │
│                          │ than the direct-demand baseline.                                                          │
