│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ targeted_transit_paths                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Keep the direct-demand linear reward, and add only demand-conditioned two-hop             │
│                          │ interactions. A path \(i \to j \to k\) is rewarded only when \(t > 0\), with its reward   │
│                          │ scaled by how strongly demand supports the incoming and outgoing legs at the intermediate │
│                          │ node. The normalized inbound/outbound shares make the profile comparable across nodes and │
│                          │ prevent generic two-hop paths from receiving the same reward. The interaction set is at   │
│                          │ most \(n(n-1)(n-2)\), within the term limit, and avoids the broader shared-endpoint and   │
│                          │ reciprocal-link penalties that performed worse.                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
