│ patch_description        │ Measure relay usefulness using the share of traffic entering node j that comes from i and │
│                          │ the share leaving j that goes to k. The current inbound factor divides by i’s total       │
│                          │ outgoing traffic, which can favor links that are common destinations for i without        │
│                          │ establishing that j is a meaningful receiving relay. Normalizing by j’s incoming traffic  │
│                          │ instead makes the path-specific factor reflect both sides of the relay. Keep the existing │
│                          │ small background reward and congestion discount so the change adjusts, rather than        │
│                          │ replaces, the current two-hop signal.                                                     │
