│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ relay_load_balance                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This approach estimates whether a demand can use a selected two-link route, then rewards  │
│                          │ that route only when both links are present. It combines those path-completion rewards    │
│                          │ with direct-link value and a mild congestion penalty for pairs of links that share a      │
│                          │ heavily loaded endpoint. Demand is normalized using a blend of peak and positive-traffic  │
│                          │ mean, so a few exceptionally large entries are less likely to suppress the rest of the    │
│                          │ signal. The resulting sparse, demand-conditioned terms aim to encourage useful relays     │
│                          │ without making every two-hop path equally attractive.                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0015                                                                                   │
