│ patch_name               │ relay-aware-two-hop                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach gives every possible two-hop relay the same bonus for an OD pair,    │
│                          │ regardless of whether demand supports either leg. This version keeps the direct-demand    │
│                          │ signal and degree-penalty weight, but scales each two-hop bonus by a bounded              │
│                          │ relay-connectivity factor: the geometric mean of the source’s demand share to the relay   │
│                          │ and the relay’s demand share to the destination, with a modest floor for plausible routes │
│                          │ that lack direct-leg evidence. The factor is capped at 1, and the path coefficient        │
│                          │ remains modest to avoid letting accumulated route bonuses overwhelm direct-link evidence. │
