│ patch_description        │ Keep the existing set of demand-supported two-hop paths and their overall scale, but      │
│                          │ discount paths through high-traffic relay nodes. A relay’s row-plus-column demand is a    │
│                          │ simple proxy for how much transit load it may already need to carry; the stronger `1 / (1 │
│                          │ + node_load / max_node_load)` discount tests whether avoiding busy relays improves the    │
│                          │ typical as well as best sampled topology. This adds no quadratic terms and leaves         │
│                          │ direct-link rewards and degree penalties unchanged.                                       │
